quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  5,42,"(They are) listeners of falsehood, (and) consumers of the unlawful. If they come to you, you can either judge between them or disregard them. If you disregard them, they shall not harm you in any way. But if you (decide to) judge, judge between them with justice. Indeed, Allah loves the just."
  5,43,"And how should they make you their judge when they (already) have the Torah with them, which contains Allah’s judgement? Yet they turn their backs after that. And they are not believers."
  5,44,"Indeed, We sent down the Torah, containing guidance and light, by which the prophets who had submitted themselves (to Allah) judged the Jews. So, too, did the rabbis and scholars (give the judgements) according to Allah’s Book, as they were entrusted to preserve and to which they were (made) witnesses. So, do not fear the people but fear Me, and do not sell My revelations for a small gain. And those who do not judge according to what Allah has revealed, it is they who are the disbelievers."
  5,45,"And We ordained for them in this (Book, the Torah): ‘A life for a life, an eye for an eye, a nose for a nose, an ear for an ear, a tooth for a tooth and equal retaliation for wounds. But whoever waives it charitably, it shall be an atonement for him. And those who do not judge according to what Allah has revealed, it is they who are the transgressors."
